COPY public.exercise_steps (id, exercise_id, order_num, text, text_en_us) FROM stdin;
9865	1	1	While holding the upper arms stationary, curl the weights forward while contracting the biceps as you breathe out.	While holding the upper arms stationary, curl the weights forward while contracting the biceps as you breathe out.
9866	1	2	Continue the movement until your biceps are fully contracted and the bar is at shoulder level.	Continue the movement until your biceps are fully contracted and the bar is at shoulder level.
9867	1	3	Hold the contracted position for a second and squeeze the biceps hard.	Hold the contracted position for a second and squeeze the biceps hard.
9868	1	4	Slowly bring the weight back down to the starting position.	Slowly bring the weight back down to the starting position.
9869	2	1	Stand up straight with a dumbbell in each hand at arm's length.	Stand up straight with a dumbbell in each hand at arm's length.
9870	2	2	Raise one dumbbell and twist your forearm until it is vertical and your palm faces the shoulder.	Raise one dumbbell and twist your forearm until it is vertical and your palm faces the shoulder.
9871	2	3	Lower to original position and repeat with opposite arm	Lower to original position and repeat with opposite arm
9872	3	1	Hold the dumbbells with a neutral grip (thumbs facing the ceiling).	Hold the dumbbells with a neutral grip (thumbs facing the ceiling).
9873	3	2	Slowly lift the dumbbell up to chest height	Slowly lift the dumbbell up to chest height
9874	3	3	Return to starting position and repeat.	Return to starting position and repeat.
9875	4	1	Lay flat on the bench with your feet on the ground. With straight arms unrack the bar.	Lay flat on the bench with your feet on the ground. With straight arms unrack the bar.
9876	4	2	Lower the bar to your mid chest	Lower the bar to your mid chest
9877	4	3	Raise the bar until you've locked your elbows.	Raise the bar until you've locked your elbows.
9878	5	1	Hold your body with arms locked above the equipment	Hold your body with arms locked above the equipment
9879	5	2	Lower your body slowly while leaning forward, flare out your elbows	Lower your body slowly while leaning forward, flare out your elbows
9880	5	3	Raise your body above the bars until your arms are locked.	Raise your body above the bars until your arms are locked.
9881	7	1	Lay flat on the bench and place your feet on the ground.	Lay flat on the bench and place your feet on the ground.
9882	7	2	Begin the exercise with the dumbbells held together above your chest, elbows slightly bent.	Begin the exercise with the dumbbells held together above your chest, elbows slightly bent.
9883	7	3	Simultaneously lower the weights to either side.	Simultaneously lower the weights to either side.
9884	7	4	Pause when the weights are parallel to the bench, then raise your arms to the starting position.	Pause when the weights are parallel to the bench, then raise your arms to the starting position.
9885	8	1	Stand with your feet shoulder-width apart. Maintain the natural arch in your back, squeezing your shoulder blades and raising your chest.	Stand with your feet shoulder-width apart. Maintain the natural arch in your back, squeezing your shoulder blades and raising your chest.
9886	8	2	Grip the bar across your shoulders and support it on your upper back. Unwrack the bar by straightening your legs, and take a step back.	Grip the bar across your shoulders and support it on your upper back. Unwrack the bar by straightening your legs, and take a step back.
9887	8	3	Bend your knees as you lower the weight without altering the form of your back until your hips are below your knees.	Bend your knees as you lower the weight without altering the form of your back until your hips are below your knees.
9888	8	4	Raise the bar back to starting position, lift with your legs and exhale at the top.	Raise the bar back to starting position, lift with your legs and exhale at the top.
9889	9	1	Place your legs on the platform with your feet at shoulder width.	Place your legs on the platform with your feet at shoulder width.
9890	9	2	Release the weight and extend your legs fully, without locking your knees.	Release the weight and extend your legs fully, without locking your knees.
9891	9	3	Lower the weight until your legs are at a 90° angle (but DO NOT allow your butt and lower back to rise off of the pad. This will put your lower back in a rounded position, which is very dangerous.)	Lower the weight until your legs are at a 90° angle (but DO NOT allow your butt and lower back to rise off of the pad. This will put your lower back in a rounded position, which is very dangerous.)
9892	9	4	Raise the weight back to starting position.	Raise the weight back to starting position.
9893	10	1	Sit on the machine with your back against the cushion and adjust the machine you are using so that your knees are at a 90 degree angle at the starting position.	Sit on the machine with your back against the cushion and adjust the machine you are using so that your knees are at a 90 degree angle at the starting position.
9894	10	2	Raise the weight by extending your knees outward, then lower your leg to the starting position. Both movements should be done in a slow, controlled motion.	Raise the weight by extending your knees outward, then lower your leg to the starting position. Both movements should be done in a slow, controlled motion.
9895	11	1	Hold the weight tucked into your upper chest area, keeping your elbows in. Your feet should be slightly wider than shoulder width.	Hold the weight tucked into your upper chest area, keeping your elbows in. Your feet should be slightly wider than shoulder width.
9896	11	2	Sink down into the squat, keeping your elbows inside the track of your knees.	Sink down into the squat, keeping your elbows inside the track of your knees.
9897	11	3	Push through your heels while keeping your chest up and return to starting position.	Push through your heels while keeping your chest up and return to starting position.
9898	12	1	Sit on a bench with dumbbells in both hands, palms facing your body, back straight.	Sit on a bench with dumbbells in both hands, palms facing your body, back straight.
9899	12	2	Elevate your shoulders and hold the contracted position at the apex of the motion.	Elevate your shoulders and hold the contracted position at the apex of the motion.
9900	12	3	Slowly lower your shoulders back to starting position.	Slowly lower your shoulders back to starting position.
9901	16	1	Sit on the bench and hold a dumbbell with both hands. Raise the dumbbell overhead at arms length, holding the weight up with the palms of your hands.	Sit on the bench and hold a dumbbell with both hands. Raise the dumbbell overhead at arms length, holding the weight up with the palms of your hands.
9902	16	2	Keep your elbows in while you lower the weight behind your head, your upper arms stationary.	Keep your elbows in while you lower the weight behind your head, your upper arms stationary.
9903	16	3	Raise the weight back to starting position.	Raise the weight back to starting position.
9904	17	1	Grip the pulley bar with palms facing down at shoulder width.	Grip the pulley bar with palms facing down at shoulder width.
9905	17	2	Stand straight with a small forward incline. Keep your upper arms close to your body, and slowly bring the pulley bar down until your arms are fully extended.	Stand straight with a small forward incline. Keep your upper arms close to your body, and slowly bring the pulley bar down until your arms are fully extended.
9906	17	3	Pause when you are at the contracted position of the motion, then slowly raise the pulley bar back to the starting point.	Pause when you are at the contracted position of the motion, then slowly raise the pulley bar back to the starting point.
9907	18	1	Grip the edge of the bench with your hands, Keep your feet together and legs straight.	Grip the edge of the bench with your hands, Keep your feet together and legs straight.
9908	18	2	Lower your body straight down.	Lower your body straight down.
9909	18	3	Slowly press back up to the starting point.	Slowly press back up to the starting point.
9910	18	4	TIP: Make this harder by raising your feet off the floor and adding weight.	TIP: Make this harder by raising your feet off the floor and adding weight.
9911	20	1	Stand up straight with dumbbells at either side, palms facing your hips.	Stand up straight with dumbbells at either side, palms facing your hips.
9912	20	2	Raise your arms on either side with a slight bend in your elbow until they are parallel with the floor. Pause at the top of the motion.	Raise your arms on either side with a slight bend in your elbow until they are parallel with the floor. Pause at the top of the motion.
9913	20	3	Slowly return your arms down to starting position.	Slowly return your arms down to starting position.
9914	21	1	With dumbbells in either hand, bend your knees with your feet slightly bowed out. Arch your back above your knees, and start with the weights touching in front of your chest.	With dumbbells in either hand, bend your knees with your feet slightly bowed out. Arch your back above your knees, and start with the weights touching in front of your chest.
9915	21	2	With bent elbows, raise your arms up to shoulder level, pausing at the at the end of the motion.	With bent elbows, raise your arms up to shoulder level, pausing at the at the end of the motion.
9916	21	3	Slowly lower your arms back to starting position.	Slowly lower your arms back to starting position.
9917	22	1	Facing the pulley, pull the weight towards you while keeping your arms parallel to the ground.	Facing the pulley, pull the weight towards you while keeping your arms parallel to the ground.
9918	22	2	Pull your hands back to both sides of your head and hold the position.	Pull your hands back to both sides of your head and hold the position.
9919	22	3	Slowly return weight to starting position. Repeat.	Slowly return weight to starting position. Repeat.
9920	23	1	Grip the bar with the palms facing forward, your hands need to be spaced out at a distance wider than shoulder width.	Grip the bar with the palms facing forward, your hands need to be spaced out at a distance wider than shoulder width.
9921	23	2	As you have both arms extended in front of you holding the bar, bring your torso back around 30 degrees while sticking your chest out.	As you have both arms extended in front of you holding the bar, bring your torso back around 30 degrees while sticking your chest out.
9922	23	3	Pull the bar down to about chin level or a little lower in a smooth movement whilst squeezing the shoulder blades together.	Pull the bar down to about chin level or a little lower in a smooth movement whilst squeezing the shoulder blades together.
9923	23	4	After a second of squeezing, slowly raise the bar back to the starting position when your arms are fully extended.	After a second of squeezing, slowly raise the bar back to the starting position when your arms are fully extended.
9924	24	1	Sit with your back straight on the machine and grip the handles.	Sit with your back straight on the machine and grip the handles.
9925	24	2	Pull the handles back using your arms. Your legs and torso should be at a 90° angle. Push out your chest.	Pull the handles back using your arms. Your legs and torso should be at a 90° angle. Push out your chest.
9926	24	3	Pull the handles towards your body until your hands are beside your abdomen.	Pull the handles towards your body until your hands are beside your abdomen.
9927	25	1	Grasp the bar with an overhand grip, arms and shoulders fully extended.	Grasp the bar with an overhand grip, arms and shoulders fully extended.
9928	25	2	Pull your body up until your chin is above the bar.	Pull your body up until your chin is above the bar.
9929	25	3	Lower your body back to starting position.	Lower your body back to starting position.
9930	26	1	Grab both dumbbells and hinge forward at the hips. Make sure you keep a flat back.	Grab both dumbbells and hinge forward at the hips. Make sure you keep a flat back.
9931	26	2	The closer your torso is to parallel with the ground the longer the range of motion will be at your shoulder. The better the results you'll get from the exercise.	The closer your torso is to parallel with the ground the longer the range of motion will be at your shoulder. The better the results you'll get from the exercise.
9932	26	3	Let your arms hang freely, and then pull your elbow joint straight back toward the ceiling.	Let your arms hang freely, and then pull your elbow joint straight back toward the ceiling.
9933	27	1	Stand with a barbell at your shins with your feet shoulder width apart.	Stand with a barbell at your shins with your feet shoulder width apart.
9934	27	2	Bend forward at your hips and keep your knees as fully extended as possible.	Bend forward at your hips and keep your knees as fully extended as possible.
9935	27	3	Grab the barbell and then extend your hips while maintaining a straight back.	Grab the barbell and then extend your hips while maintaining a straight back.
9936	27	4	From the standing position, lower the weight in a controlled manner.	From the standing position, lower the weight in a controlled manner.
9937	27	5	You can either lower the weight to the floor or before you touch the floor, depending on your mobility.	You can either lower the weight to the floor or before you touch the floor, depending on your mobility.
10079	76	3	Slowly lower until you are in the starting position and repeat.	Slowly lower until you are in the starting position and repeat.
9938	28	1	Lay down on the machine, placing your legs beneath the padded lever. Position your legs so that the padded lever is below your calve muscles.	Lay down on the machine, placing your legs beneath the padded lever. Position your legs so that the padded lever is below your calve muscles.
9939	28	2	Support yourself by grabbing the side handles of the machine, and slowly raise the weight with your legs, toes pointed straight.	Support yourself by grabbing the side handles of the machine, and slowly raise the weight with your legs, toes pointed straight.
9940	28	3	Pause at the apex of the motion, then slowly return to starting position.	Pause at the apex of the motion, then slowly return to starting position.
9941	29	1	Lie down with your knees bent and your feet flat on the floor.	Lie down with your knees bent and your feet flat on the floor.
9942	29	2	Push your hips up so that your butt is elevated and your back straight.	Push your hips up so that your butt is elevated and your back straight.
9943	29	3	Tense your glutes and raise your hips towards the ceiling.	Tense your glutes and raise your hips towards the ceiling.
9944	29	4	Once you are at the highest point you can manage, hold the position for a few seconds, and then slowly return to the starting position	Once you are at the highest point you can manage, hold the position for a few seconds, and then slowly return to the starting position
9945	30	1	Sit on the ground with a bench behind you. Have the barbell over your legs just above your hips.	Sit on the ground with a bench behind you. Have the barbell over your legs just above your hips.
9946	30	2	Lean back against the bench so that your shoulders are resting upon it, stretch your arms out to either side using the bench as support.	Lean back against the bench so that your shoulders are resting upon it, stretch your arms out to either side using the bench as support.
9947	30	3	Raise the weight by driving through your feet and extending your hips upwards. Support the weight with your shoulders and feet.	Raise the weight by driving through your feet and extending your hips upwards. Support the weight with your shoulders and feet.
9948	30	4	Slowly extend as far as you can, and then slowly return to the starting position.	Slowly extend as far as you can, and then slowly return to the starting position.
9949	31	1	Stand straight and hold the barbell behind you using a pronated grip with your hands and feet shoulder-width apart.	Stand straight and hold the barbell behind you using a pronated grip with your hands and feet shoulder-width apart.
9950	31	2	Slowly curl your wrists in a semi-circular motion upwards.	Slowly curl your wrists in a semi-circular motion upwards.
9951	31	3	Hold the barbell at the apex of the motion and then slowly lower the barbell back down to starting position.	Hold the barbell at the apex of the motion and then slowly lower the barbell back down to starting position.
9952	32	1	Grip the dumbbell with your palm facing upwards with your forearm rested against the bench.	Grip the dumbbell with your palm facing upwards with your forearm rested against the bench.
9953	32	2	Slowly curl your wrist upwards in a semicircular motion.	Slowly curl your wrist upwards in a semicircular motion.
